    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Crowns & Owls is a London-based directing and photography collective of three: Thomas Harrison (director), James-Alexander Adair (DOP), and Rory Martinez (producer/creative director). Founded c.2011 in Leeds as Brown Bread Films, rebranded and relocated to London, registered Ltd company (Companies House 07692399). Represented by Iconoclast. Senior creative collective level, 13+ years active; clients include Nike (Marcus Rashford, Emma Raducanu), Adidas, Lil Yachty, Slowthai, James Blake, Chase and Status, Ted Baker, River Island, Diesel, Flannels. Won Best R&B/Soul Video UKMVAs 2023 (Lil Yachty, Say Something). Site bio states 'Moving image, photography and creative direction.' Originally filmmakers; photography a secondary capability added over time. Autonomy 4: established, senior-level collective operating autonomously with major brand clients, small 3-person team doing hands-on work across preproduction through delivery.",
      "source_url": "https://www.crownsandowls.com/information/",
